Z||000000||Hank is Here||07-09-2001||07:26 AM||||<BR>Well I am proud to say that I am the first forum member to meet Cliff Pennock in person. This weekend I made a trip to Amsterdam, then a side trip to Haarlem to meet Cliff.  All I can say that he is a great guy, who seems to have endless hobbies.  He drove me to the local Fiero shop (and yes there is a local Fiero shop in The Netherlands).  At the shop they had an SBC swap that was just finished, some convertibles they made themselves, their own interiors and dashes; also a rear window/roof spoiler.  I was expecting to see some crazy European motor swaps but they still stuck to the American GM motors.  <BR>Also I must say the new gauges that Cliff has developed is great.  For those of you that like the bells and whistles of modern cars you will want this dash. The dash is able to display 0-60 times automatically, even able to calculate average sped, you can even program it to greet you when you start the car.  I have just covered a FEW of the features this dash has--it is GREAT   Good job Cliff!<BR>Also then Cliff and I had a chance to sit back and have a beer and just talk about misc. stuff.<P>Glad to have met you Cliff<P>Hank is Here<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||07-09-2001||07:47 AM||||Sorry I didn't have time to wash my car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Did you stay in Amsterdam? Or did you take a trip back to Belgium? I was kinda worried that you wouldn't be able to find a place to stay and that you would be wandering the streets of Amsterdam at night.<P>(edited for spelling correction)<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
